From 6482ea625a0a8effb4fc8f1eed3529e0e9de9d70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy1210 <andy1210@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:42:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 144/149] usb: dwc3: qcom: Keep the VBUS override clear unless
 the role is device

The QSCRATCH VBUS override is what tells the controller about a device
session; dwc3-qcom sets and clears it from the pre_set_role and
pre_run_stop glue hooks. Two cases leave it set with no host attached:

- dwc3_qcom_set_role_notifier() decides from the role it leaves, not
  the one it enters, so host -> none (and none -> host) set the
  override.
- dwc3_qcom_run_stop_notifier() sets it on every pullup, so binding a
  UDC from userspace after the role switch reported "none" (a gadget
  rebound around system sleep, a function added to a configfs gadget)
  sets it again.

With the override set and no cable, the controller keeps D+ pulled up
on an empty port and treats a later attach as a continuation of the old
session: there is no disconnect and no new connect. Set the override
exactly when the role becomes device, and let a pullup restore it only
while the role is device. Until the role switch first reports, the role
is device (as before), so a gadget bound early in boot still connects.

dr_mode "peripheral" is unchanged: its role is device from probe on.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c | 17 +++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
index ac68b4218b56..1e4d0471ce0f 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
@@ -570,10 +570,12 @@ static void dwc3_qcom_set_role_notifier(struct dwc3 *dwc, enum usb_role next_rol
 		return;
 	}
 
-	if (qcom->current_role == USB_ROLE_DEVICE)
-		dwc3_qcom_vbus_override_enable(qcom, false);
-	else if (qcom->current_role != USB_ROLE_DEVICE)
-		dwc3_qcom_vbus_override_enable(qcom, true);
+	/*
+	 * The controller sees a session only while it is a device: a role
+	 * switch to "none" is the cable going away, and clearing the override
+	 * is what makes the controller report the disconnect.
+	 */
+	dwc3_qcom_vbus_override_enable(qcom, next_role == USB_ROLE_DEVICE);
 
 	pm_runtime_mark_last_busy(qcom->dev);
 	pm_runtime_put_sync(qcom->dev);
@@ -593,9 +595,12 @@ static void dwc3_qcom_run_stop_notifier(struct dwc3 *dwc, bool is_on)
 	 * When autosuspend is enabled and controller goes to suspend
 	 * after removing UDC from userspace, the next UDC write needs
 	 * setting of QSCRATCH VBUS_VALID to "1" to generate a connect
-	 * done event.
+	 * done event. Only do so while the role is "device": with no
+	 * cable the override must stay clear until the role switch
+	 * reports a host, or the controller pulls D+ up on an empty
+	 * port and never sees the next attach as a new session.
 	 */
-	if (!is_on)
+	if (!is_on || qcom->current_role != USB_ROLE_DEVICE)
 		return;
 
 	dwc3_qcom_vbus_override_enable(qcom, true);
